Local adaptation of upstream m1n1 commit
f7124b8d42bcdd44131b4a455ad32e2f98fde166 for the full14 local baseline.
Original upstream change: Sven Peter <sven@svenpeter.dev> (MIT-licensed m1n1).
Provenance: upstream section/mapping idea; AI-assisted Debian project work;
not submitted upstream. Included in the local offline build with patch 0016.

This focused backport keeps the pinned baseline's initial CPU-start/reset
semantics and 32-CPU guards; it intentionally does not import the newer
`smp_reset_stacks[]` re-entry implementation. The local adaptation additionally
places both secondary stack-pointer tables in `.data.smp_shared`, because the
secondary reads `secondary_stacks[smp_id()]` before enabling its MMU. The DATA
alignment is performed before `_data_start` so Mach-O DATA vmaddr/vmsize do not
include an unrepresented alignment gap. Only the two reset-pointer
`dc_civac_range()` calls are removed; the existing `dsb sy` and all guards stay.

Offline-tested backport; no native safety claim.
